hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"781","Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning al-Qattan - narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, he said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr say: I was asked about the two who invoke curses whether they are separated, during the rule of Ibn al-Zubayr, and I did not know what to say. So I stood from my place to the house of Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) and said: Abu Abd al-Rahman, are the two who invoke curses separated? He said: Glory be to Allah, yes. The first who asked about that was so-and-so son of so-and-so. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man among us who sees his wife in indecency? If he speaks, he speaks of a grave matter, and if he is silent, he is silent over the like of that! He said: So he did not answer him. He said: When the next day came he came to him and said: That which I asked about, I have been afflicted with it. So Allah sent down this verse in Surat al-Nur: And those who accuse their wives, until it reached: and the fifth, that the anger of Allah be upon her if he is of the truthful. So he began with the man, admonishing him and reminding him, and informing him that the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter. So he said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I have not lied. Then he turned to the woman, admonishing her and reminding her, and informing her that the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter. So she said: By the One who sent you with the truth, he is indeed a liar. He said: So he began with the man, and he testified four testimonies by Allah that he is of the truthful, and the fifth that the curse of Allah be upon him if he is of the liars. Then he turned to the woman, and she testified four testimonies by Allah that he is of the liars, and the fifth that the anger of Allah be upon her if he is of the truthful. Then he separated between them."
"782","al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated between the two who invoke curses, and said: Your account is upon Allah; one of you is lying; there is no way for you to her. He said: O Messenger of Allah, my wealth? He said: You have no wealth from her; if you were truthful to her, then it is for what you made lawful of her private part, and if you lied, then that is further from it for you."
"783","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that a man invoked curses against his wife and disowned her child, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated between them, and attached the child to the woman."
"784","al-Rabi ibn Sulayman informed us that Ibn Wahb narrated to them, he said: Ibn Abi al-Zinad informed me, from his father, he said: al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Abdillah ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invoked curses between al-Ajlani and his wife, and she was pregnant."
"785","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Sad, that Uwaymir came to Asim ibn Adi and mentioned part of the hadith. He said: So he invoked curses against her, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you keep her, you have wronged her. He said: So he divorced her, and it became afterwards a practice for those who invoked curses after them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Watch; if she brings him dark, intensely black-eyed, large-buttocked, thick-legged, then I do not think Uwaymir but that he told the truth; and if she brings him reddish as though a small gecko, then I do not think Uwaymir but that he lied. He said: So she brought him according to the description the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) described, confirming Uwaymir. He said: And he was afterwards attributed to his mother."
"786","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Israil, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both). He said: And Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, he said: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A woman accepted Islam in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then she married. So her husband came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I had accepted Islam along with her, and she knew of my Islam. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took her from her latter husband and returned her to her first husband."
"787","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman - meaning Ibn Sulayman ibn al-Ghasil - narrated to us, from Hamzah ibn Abi Usayd, from Abu Usayd, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we set out to a garden called al-Shawt, until we reached two gardens. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sit here. Then he entered, and al-Jawniyyah had been brought and lodged in the palm-house: Umaymah bint al-Numan ibn Sharahil, with a nurse caring for her. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her, he said: Give yourself to me. She said: Does a queen give herself to a commoner? He said: So he reached out his hand to place it upon her to calm her, and she said: I seek refuge in Allah from you. He said: You have sought refuge in a place of refuge. Then he came out to us and said: O Abu Usayd, clothe her with two razqiyyah garments and take her to her family."
